  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Haiti emergency response to hurricane Melissa 2025Haiti emergency response to hurricane Melissa 2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the aftermath of Hurricane Melissa, Haiti has experienced extensive flooding, shelter destruction, and widespread displacement across several departments. In response to this urgent humanitarian situation, the Melissa Emergency Response Project is designed to provide life-saving assistance to the most affected populations in three departments identified through official assessments as most severely affected: Grande-Anse, Artibonite, and South (Sud) departments, and IOM has emergency teams based in Sud and Artibonite departments. The response is structured around three integrated components. Shelter Support and Rehabilitation to provide emergency shelters kits through the Common Pipeline system and Shelter Rehabilitation Kits, engaging skilled local community members in Cash-for-Work activities to support technical assessment and rehabilitation of damaged houses. This will contribute to enhancing the communities&apos; emergency livelihoods in the wake of the shock. Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene (WASH) services to improve access to hygiene, safe water and sanitation through restoration of water points, desludging and cleaning drainage channels, distribution of hygiene kits, and promotion of hygiene practices to prevent disease outbreaks. Protection and immediate Psychological First Aid and basic protection measures, prioritizing vulnerable groups such as children, female-headed households, the elderly, and persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
